   <bpmn:task id="Bridge_2_ea67" name="Here is the transition sentence connecting Process A and Process B, followed by the integrated business process design you requested.&#10;&#10;### Transition Sentence&#10;**&quot;Once the IP approves the transaction request, the payment process is initiated, leading to the Payment Office generating the vendor report and client invoices, which subsequently triggers the archiving and reconciliation activities by the Registry and Accounts Receivable departments.&quot;**&#10;&#10;***&#10;&#10;### Integrated Business Process Design&#10;**Title:** Integrated Vendor Payment, Client Invoicing, and Invoice Archiving Workflow&#10;&#10;**Roles:**&#10;*   **Payment Office:** Initiates payments and generates reports.&#10;*   **Vendor:** Receives payment.&#10;*   **Clients:** Receives invoices.&#10;*   **Registry Office:** Archives physical records.&#10;*   **Accounts Receivable Department:** Manages client billing and financial reconciliation.&#10;&#10;**Process Flow:**&#10;&#10;1.  **Payment Initiation (Payment Office):**&#10;    *   At the end of the week, the **Payment Office** generates a consolidated **Payment Report**.&#10;    *   The office processes the **Vendor Payment** based on this report.&#10;&#10;2.  **Client Invoicing (Accounts Receivable Department):**&#10;    *   Simultaneously, the **Accounts Receivable Department** generates monthly invoices for **Clients**.&#10;    *   A fixed charge of **$35 per invoice** is applied, and the client is notified.&#10;&#10;3.  **Distribution &amp; Notification:**&#10;    *   The **Payment Office** sends the payment report and payment invoice automatically to **Clients**.&#10;    *   The **Payment Office** sends the payment report to the **Registry Office** and the **Accounts Receivable Department**.&#10;&#10;4.  **Decision Point: Invoice Payment Status**&#10;    *   **Check:** Has the client payment been received/confirmed?&#10;        *   **Outcome 1 (Paid):** Proceed to Step 5 (Archiving &amp; Reconciliation).&#10;        *   **Outcome 2 (Unpaid):** Trigger a &quot;Payment Tracking&quot; sub-process (initiated by the Registry Office) until the status changes to &quot;Paid.&quot;&#10;&#10;5.  **Archiving &amp; Tracking (Registry Office):**&#10;    *   The **Registry Office** selects the paper-based invoices marked as &quot;Paid.&quot;&#10;    *   They **archive invoices** per vendor, then per payment data.&#10;    *   They formally **track down the payment** to confirm the transaction is fully closed." /><bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P2B_2" sourceRef="atom_1_Task_3" targetRef="Bridge_2_ea67" /><bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_B2C_2" sourceRef="Bridge_2_ea67" targetRef="atom_2_sid-A5093785-9337-44F9-BA57-6837E2F0DA1B" /></bpmn:process>
